  "articleBody": "Installing marble tile is a delicate job, and avoiding common mistakes can save you a lot of grief (and money!). One major slip-up is using the wrong mortar or grout. Marble is a natural stone, and it can react poorly with certain materials, leading to staining or discoloration, so you need products specifically designed for natural stone. Another big no-no is installing over an uneven subfloor. Marble is less forgiving than other tiles, and an uneven surface will result in lippage – where one tile edge is higher than another – or even cracks. Don't forget to dry-fit your tiles and plan your layout, accounting for the natural variations in color and veining that marble has; skipping this step can lead to a patchy look. Also, be super careful with cleaning during and after installation; abrasive cleaners or residues can easily scratch or etch the beautiful finish. If you're nervous about any of these steps, especially for large-format tiles or a wet area like a shower, getting a professional involved is a smart move. They have the experience to prevent these issues and ensure a flawless finish.",
